# Rust build artifacts
# Isolated working copies of extracted upstream repositories, never dependency overrides.
/.extracted/
/target/
# A cargo target dir pointed at the repo root instead of target/ (an ad-hoc
# `--target-dir .`, or `CARGO_TARGET_DIR=..` from a crate subdirectory) writes
# its profile dirs and rustc probe here. That is always a mistake — the build
# location is target/, which the Makefile exports — but it is a silent one:
# 3.9 GB landed here on 2026-09-23 while the internal disk was already failing
# builds with ENOSPC. Ignored so it never rides along in a commit; `du -sh
# debug release` at the repo root is how you notice it, and `make
# check-build-space` fails a build before the volume does.
/debug/
/release/
/.rustc_info.json
desktop/src-tauri/target/
native/**/.build/
**/*.rs.bk
*.pdb

# Runtime data (tasks, threads, observations, checkpoints, pause states)
# Keep directory structure traversable, but ignore files by default.
.magician_data/
magician_data_v3/**
!magician_data_v3/**/
# Allowlisted runtime files to keep in git:
# Scoped agent definitions = the live anonymous/default roster seed. They carry
# per-deployment capability grants that drift ahead of the templates (and some
# agents have no template at all). The bootstrap materializer only writes a
# scoped def when one is ABSENT, so these are load-bearing seed, not regenerable
# duplicates — keep them tracked.
!magician_data_v3/scopes/anonymous/default/agent_runtime/agents/*/definition.agent.yaml
# ...except keka-clocker: user-specific personal automation (hardcoded HR portal
# + personal account). Keep it out of the shipped seed.
magician_data_v3/scopes/anonymous/default/agent_runtime/agents/keka-clocker/definition.agent.yaml
# Generic scoped program spec used by the Harness SRE seed. Other live program
# docs remain runtime-owned and ignored unless explicitly allowlisted.
!magician_data_v3/scopes/anonymous/default/programs/harness_reliability.md
# The outward charter the `ambassador` seed reads every cycle. It ships UNFILLED
# on purpose — the agent treats an unfilled section as empty and sends nothing —
# so what is tracked here is the shape an operator fills in, not company content.
!magician_data_v3/scopes/anonymous/default/programs/outward_charter.md
# Scoped trust policies + the rest of the per-scope agent_runtime/system/ tree are
# regenerated at first scope access from system/trust_policy_templates/ (with a
# compiled-in fallback), so nothing there needs to be tracked.
!magician_data_v3/system/**
# .env template ships in the seed; operators copy it to the runtime root as .env.
!magician_data_v3/.env.example
# operator-config template ships in the seed; operators copy it to the runtime
# root as operator-config.yaml (read by both magician + skillshub setup).
!magician_data_v3/operator-config.template.yaml
# LLM pricing template ships in the seed; operators copy it to the runtime
# root as llm_pricing.json (effective-dated rates layered over the built-in
# pricing table). Dev checkouts load the template directly as the fallback.
!magician_data_v3/llm_pricing.template.json
magician_data_v3/system/wake_up_queue.json
magician_data_v3/scopes/**/.artifact_v2.lock

# AgentSkills v1 runtime trees — regenerated by `make -C skillshub install-*`
# from the skillshub/ source folder. Never commit; always regenerate.
magician_data_v3/system/skills/
magician_data_v3/scopes/*/*/skills/

# Per-skill build artifacts under skillshub/<name>/bin/ — populated by
# `make setup-*` (e.g. setup-agent-browser deploys agent-browser into
# skillshub/browser/bin/). Browser's tracked patch is the source of truth;
# native artifacts under its versioned _vendor tree are rebuilt locally.
skillshub/*/bin/
